 "letterboxd-review-1181083727": {
  "guid": "letterboxd-review-1181083727",
  "title": "Marty Supreme",
  "year": 2025,
  "rating": 4.5,
  "like": true,
  "rewatch": false,
  "watched": "2026-01-29",
  "tmdb": 1317288,
  "url": "https://letterboxd.com/martinocueto/film/marty-supreme/",
  "review": "Another great performance from Timothée, the message is good even if in our society it seems like trying to be the best and having a goal to chase is “sick” or “toxic”. Personally I can understand Marty’s stress and sometimes toxicity when it comes to the only thing that matters to him, being the best. I think the way he is arrogant and selfish shows us how actually you need to be in order to be a winner , even if nobody will like you. The other thing I love about this movie is that we get to se Timothée, other than the character he plays. The movie represents perfectly how he sees his career, himself and all that comes with it. For once we could actually see that thing that he was missing in the other movies, a touch of his personality, his way to be. Photography, music and scenes were great, nothing new to be honest.\nI really hope Timothée will keep this kind of obsession, if he does he will be the best, just like Marty.\nTyler was good too."
 },
